    "result_text": "The full test suite consists of the single `AcceptanceTest` (the other files are an abstract base and a helper) and it passes \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a **per-city** sequence, keeping each piece of logic in its proper layer:\n\n**Generation logic** \u2014 `CustomerCodeAssigner.assign()`:\n- Now derives `CITY3` from the owner's city and `LAST3` from the last name via a shared `prefix()` helper (upper-cased first three letters), eliminating the duplicated substring logic.\n- The `NNNN` sequence is now `countOwnersByCity(city) + 1` instead of the global owner count.\n\n**Per-city count** \u2014 added a `countByCity(String)` method following the existing `count()` pattern through every layer so the assigner stays thin and the query lives in the repository:\n- `OwnerRepository` interface (contract + javadoc)\n- `JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl` (JPQL) and `JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl` (SQL) for the `jpa`/`jdbc` profiles\n- `SpringDataOwnerRepository` picks it up automatically as a derived query (the active `spring-data-jpa` profile)\n- `ClinicService` / `ClinicServiceImpl` (`countOwnersByCity`, delegating to the repository, `@Transactional(readOnly = true)`)\n\n**Derived values rebuild automatically** \u2014 `Owner.getMembershipNumber()` is computed on read as `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, so it already reflects the new customer code with no code change; I only updated its javadoc example.\n\n**Documentation** \u2014 updated the `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` descriptions and examples in `openapi.yml` and the `CustomerCodeAssigner`/`Owner` javadoc to the new format.\n\nThe acceptance test (`customerCode` matching `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) passes.",
